  "docs.onet.skills": "O*NET Software Skills supplies occupation-specific tool examples mapped through explicit aliases to our glossary, scoped to each app role’s editorial skill list. In Demand tools receive app weight 3; others 2, not official O*NET ratings. Core task statements also map explicit skill aliases within that role scope (app weight 3). Knowledge adds the top five non-suppressed IM ≥ 3 subject areas; essential/transferable skills retain the top 12. Alias and course title/summary matches are application crosswalks, not course coverage certification. General work skills also need a matching course title, and office/Excel links exclude incidental mentions in technical examples. Matcher checks current catalogue skill IDs and links actual courses; requirements without courses remain visible separately and the planner reports uncovered gaps. Matching course titles and introductory levels take priority over incidental examples or instructor training.",
